---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import TokenTable from "../components/TokenTable.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Token reference"
  documentLayout="grid"
  description="All system tokens: token read from CSS in build, value resolved read from live browser."
>
  <h1>Token reference</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Each token in its two forms: the token that was written and the value that resolves right now, in the dimensions selected above.
  </p>

  <TokenTable />

  <h2>How to read the tiers</h2>
  <p>
    References point <strong>down or sideways, never up</strong>, and tier 3 cannot jump to tier 1. That is not convention: the validator enforces it. A <code>--palette-*</code> within a component's CSS is the visible sign that someone skipped the semantic layer and broke dark mode for that component alone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <span class="sk-badge" data-tone="success">component</span> tokens live on the element rather than on
    <code>:root</code>, so they are resolved here against a test element carrying the class. If one reads
    <em>unresolved in this context</em>, that is not a bug but tier 3 scoping showing through: the token does
    not exist until an element opts into it.
  </p>
</Base>
